Explanation:
• The original condition would call indent() even when siblingIndex==0 (for the very first text node),
  which led to a spurious newline before “Hello” in the failing test.
• In this version we only indent when siblingIndex > 0. In addition, if the immediately previous sibling is 
  a <br> element then we unconditionally indent so that text “wraps” appropriately.
• The rest of the code (including trim flags and escaping) remains the same.

