In our fix the TLV‐loop processes data only up to “limit” (i.e. excluding the 2–byte trailer) and the fixed–auxiliary branch is entered only when exactly 20 useful bytes remain. This ensures that when a message carries extra TLV elements (for example the driver unique ID field under subtype 0xBD) those fields are parsed and saved as expected.

