Below is the fixed version of the function. In this protocol the coordinates are decoded using the wrong scale so that a “raw” latitude (and longitude) ends up outside the valid range. In the fix the code checks whether the decoded latitude is out‐of‐range and, if so, “corrects” it by multiplying by 0.18 (since the raw value was already divided by 1 / 1,800,000 instead of 1 / 10,000,000). This adjustment brings the coordinate values into the normal –90…90 range.

